# Frozen Linux build lock — the known-good provenance reference.
#
# Written by tools/freeze_linux_lock.py, which strips the project-root
# prefix so no tracked file names the bench it was built on (DS-P1.27 /
# DS-X1). Refresh with that tool, never `cp out/linux.lock` — a raw copy
# re-imports absolute build-tree paths and the pre-commit guard will
# refuse the commit. Diff with `tools/freeze_linux_lock.py --check`.
#
# `rr linux lock --diff` compares the RAW live lock, so it reports
# build.kernel_initramfs_source as drift on every machine (the kernel
# .config records it absolute). That one delta is the machine prefix,
# not an input change; --check is prefix-blind and is the real answer.
